{title: Praise the Lord! Ye Heavens, Adore Him}
{artist: Foundling Hospital Collection (1796), Edward Osler / Franz Joseph Haydn}
{genre: Hymn, Psalm}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: F}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: praise-the-lord-ye-heavens-adore-him.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Praise_The_Lord_Ye_Heavens_Adore_Him-Austria_Haydn-Austrian_Hymn)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Praise the Lord: [C7]ye heavens, [F]a[C7]dore [F]Him;
[F]Praise Him, [C7]an[F]gels [Gm]in [G7]the [C]height.
[Dm]Sun and [C7]moon, rejoice [F]be[C7]fore [F]Him;
[Bb]Praise [F]Him, [Gm]all [F]ye [Gm]stars [G7]of [C7]light.
[C7]Praise the Lord, for He hath spoken;
[Am]Worlds His [Dm]mighty [G7]voice o[C]beyed.
[F]Laws which [Bb]ne[F]ver [Bb]shall be [Dm]bro[F]ken
[C7]For their guidance He hath [F]made.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Praise the Lord, [C7]for He [F]is [C7]glor[F]ious;
[F]Never [C7]shall [F]His [Gm]pro[G7]mise [C]fail.
[Dm]God hath [C7]made His saints [F]vic[C7]tor[F]ious;
[Bb]Sin [F]and [Gm]death [F]shall [Gm]not [G7]pre[C7]vail.
[C7]Praise the God of our salvation;
[Am]Hosts on [Dm]high, His [G7]power pro[C]claim.
[F]Heaven and [Bb]earth [F]and [Bb]all cre[Dm]a[F]tion,
[C7]Laud and magnify His [F]name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Worship, ho[C7]nor, glo[F]ry, [C7]bless[F]ing,
[F]Lord, we [C7]of[F]fer [Gm]un[G7]to [C]Thee.
[Dm]Young and [C7]old, Thy praise [F]ex[C7]press[F]ing,
[Bb]In [F]glad [Gm]ho[F]mage [Gm]bend [G7]the [C7]knee.
[C7]All the saints in Heaven adore Thee;
[Am]We would [Dm]bow be[G7]fore Thy [C]throne.
[F]As Thine [Bb]an[F]gels [Bb]serve be[Dm]fore [F]Thee,
[C7]So on earth Thy will be [F]done.
{end_of_verse}
